  Where it goes: <parent>/pom-reactor.xml and <parent>/.mvn/jvm.config, beside the repositories clone_all.py clones:

      <parent>/drishti-tools/java    drishti-rachana/java    drishti-lake/java    drishti

  Open pom-reactor.xml in IntelliJ (or run  mvn -f pom-reactor.xml clean package -DskipTests ) and the four products are one workspace.
  Each product anchors its paths on its own root (project.rootDirectory, the nearest .mvn), so it builds the same alone and here.
  The released exec pom.xml (one wrapper run per product) is unchanged.

  <parent>/.mvn/ must carry the same two files as drishti/.mvn/ (copy them; this repository's .mvn/ is that copy):
      jvm.config      the javac add-exports and add-opens flags the Drishti annotation processors need
      maven.config    -Drevision=<Drishti version>: the module poms name their parent as ${revision}, which Maven reads before any pom, so only a
                      command-line property can supply it (the property in the Drishti pom serves the root pom only). Keep it equal to drishti/.mvn/maven.config.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.ash.platform</groupId>
    <artifactId>drishti-platform-reactor</artifactId>
    <version>1</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>
    <name>Drishti platform: one reactor</name>

    <modules>
        <module>drishti-tools/java</module>
        <module>drishti-rachana/java</module>
        <module>drishti-lake/java</module>
        <module>drishti</module>
    </modules>
</project>
